ApplicationFollowUp.description:
A follow-up questionnaire sent to the candidate. Until it is answered, `questions` and `answers` are empty;
once it is, `questions` are the questions as the candidate saw them, so the answers read the same after the
workflow changes.

DefinitionError.description:
A problem with a definition. Path is a JSON path such as `workflow.stages[1].id` for code;
Message is a whole sentence for a person that names the thing and says what to do, so a screen can
show it as it is.

PublicBranding.description:
An organization's branding as its careers pages, the apply flow and the embeddable widget use it. Every part is null
for ScreenHire's default. `colors` come from the brand colour; `header` is the band in the second colour,
with white or ink text on it; image `url`s are absolute addresses on the careers board.

ScorecardAnswerEntry.description:
A question as the reviewer was asked it, and their answer. `value` is "yes" or "no" for the yes-or-no kinds, an
option id for a choice and the text for the text kinds; `values` are a multi-choice answer's option ids;
`rating` is the number picked on a 1 to 5 or 1 to 10 scale. All empty means it was not answered.
